<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Swabian-Alemannic Fastnacht</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fasnet</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Swabian-Alemannic Fastnacht, or Fasnet, is the traditional carnival of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vorarlberg">Vorarlberg</a>, held before Lent. Figures in carved wooden masks and costumes parade through the streets, and the Narrensprung of Rottweil is one of the most famous events. The custom is listed in Germany's inventory of intangible cultural heritage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/swabian-alemannic-fastnacht.jpg" alt="Swabian-Alemannic Fastnacht" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo: Andreas Praefcke · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narrenzunft_Tettnang_Hopfennarr_Narrentreffen_Me%C3%9Fkirch_2006.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
